From f28bd25d409a7fb96d690198e07ce0aa619db09f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:50:10 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp tr098] P4c: WANPPPConnection.{i}, 42 parameters

sub_entry_wandevice_wanconnectiondevice_ppp() of functions/tr098/wan_device,
plus wan_device_browse_instances_wancxdev_ppp() and the PPP half of
wan_device_get_total_entry().

Added to wanip_mtk.c rather than a second file.  The shell serves both objects
from one function pair parameterised by $targe_conn_type, and the PPP entry
calls the same wan_device_get_* helpers as the IP one for thirty of its
leaves.  A separate module would have to export those thirty helpers under a
prefix, or duplicate them and let the two copies drift.

Instance model, unchanged from the IP object: entries are the anonymous
"config entry" sections of UCI package wan, scanned in file order, stopped at
the first without an id, and the CWMP instance is id + 1.  The filter is the
only difference -- switch_mode 0 and conn_type 2.  Every entry belongs to
exactly one of the two objects, so WANIPConnection.2 and WANPPPConnection.2
are different entries and that is what the product has always reported.

Leaves that are not shared: TransportType (constant PPPoE), Username,
Password, RemoteIPAddress (ubus ptpaddress), MaxMRUSize, CurrentMRUSize
(the MTU of the l3 device) and Reset.  Stats read the l3_device ubus reports
instead of network.if<id>.device -- for PPPoE the counters live on the ppp
netdev, which is the third case of wan_device_get_eth_stats().

Permissions follow the PPP branch, not the IP one: DefaultGateway and
RemoteIPAddress are read-only, and ExternalIPAddress and DNSEnabled take the
shell's "true" setter, which accepts the write and changes nothing.

Two deliberate differences, both stated in the file:

  - Password reads back empty.  The shell returned the stored PPP password to
    whoever asked; TR-098 says this parameter reads as an empty string.
    Writing is unchanged.
  - Reset queues "ifdown; sleep 1; ifup" on the apply-service list instead of
    running it inline.  Inline, on the WAN carrying the session, the shell cut
    the connection before the response was sent and the ACS saw a timeout.

One mirrored bug: MaxMTUSize.  The PPP branch passes $iface and $device to
wan_device_get_mtu / wan_device_set_br_mtu in a function that never sets
either, so the getter answered empty and the setter range-checked the value
and then wrote the invalid path "network..mtu" -- success, no change.  Same
here.

Data model: 259 -> 301 of 783 parameters.  verify-dm-paths: phase 4 now 99/173
with 0 extras, and nothing under WANPPPConnection is left except the three
branches of P4d/P4e/P4f.  88 claims across 12 modules, 0 overlaps.

NOT BUILD-TESTED on this host: no compiler here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
